WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:06.069
David, if Donald Trump is unfortunately reelected
in November of 2020, how bad do you think

00:00:06.069 --> 00:00:08.350
his second term would be?

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:13.589
So in thinking about a Trump second term,
there are two sides to it.

00:00:13.589 --> 00:00:17.760
One is Trump is incredibly childish and vindictive.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.380
The other side is Trump is incredibly lazy.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:26.630
So I would predict that a second term Trump
would simultaneously be more unhinged and

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:32.300
brazen and authoritarian in going after his
political enemies, using executive orders

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:35.260
to do whatever he wants more frequently.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:39.899
But at the same time, I see him watching a
lot more TV and playing a lot more golf and

00:00:39.899 --> 00:00:43.200
being even lazier than he has been because
he's not gonna have anything else to campaign

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.430
for.

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:49.240
Maybe towards the end of his second term,
Trump would have a Republican nominee to campaign

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.990
for if they believe that it would be useful.

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:57.500
Remember back in two thousand eight, you didn't
see George W. Bush campaigning for John McCain

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:01.360
very much because George W. Bush's approval
rating was in the toilet.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:05.500
And it wouldn't have been a good thing for
McCain to have Bush out there prominently.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.980
So I would expect a few different things.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:12.030
Trump's not going to have his rallies, so
he'll watch more TV and play more golf.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:14.520
He'll feed his ego on Twitter.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:19.180
In terms of what he will get done, certainly
Donald Trump will continue to get a lot done

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:25.580
on judges because Trump is just a tool in
Mitch McConnell's toolbox, so to speak, when

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:26.580
it comes to judges.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:27.960
And they will continue.

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:33.900
They may get more Supreme Court justices on
the court, depending on who goes and who stays

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:35.500
in Trump's second term.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:37.300
They will keep putting more federal judges
in.

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:42.730
And so no doubt, if Trump is given four more
years, laziness aside, tweeting aside, his

00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:47.790
effect on the Jewish judiciary is going to
be absolutely damaging for decades to come.

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:49.320
That's going to continue.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:53.460
Beyond that, I don't believe you will see
Trump do much of significance when it comes

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.320
to big policy achievements.

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:59.310
I don't think Trump will get anything done
on health care the way he promised to do during

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:01.020
his first term.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:04.630
And a lot of the reason is Trump doesn't really
believe in what he's doing.

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:12.110
You know, Trump put together this faux conservative
ideology where he pretended to care about

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:16.380
debt and he pretended to care about, you know,
stopping abortion and stuff.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.660
He didn't care about his entire life.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:22.000
And Trump's ideology is not a conservative
ideology.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.000
It's what I call.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:28.990
And so a sort of imbecilic reactionary ideology
where Trump just is very opinionated.

00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:31.980
And in some cases he is very reactionary in
other cases.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:36.240
He's libertarian in the sense that he doesn't
care what people do.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:40.940
He's taking positions on some of these issues
because he's figured out that it appeals to

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:42.840
evangelical and other right wing voters.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:49.910
So because Donald Trump doesn't really have
a very important or significant political

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:54.990
ideology as such, I think Trump will not get
much done at all.

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:57.790
And he's just going to kind of hang out now.

00:02:57.790 --> 00:03:04.930
His authoritarianism, combined with his vindictive
nature to me, suggest that in addition to

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:09.470
helping Mitch McConnell get his judges in,
maybe trying to get some kind of tax cuts

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:16.980
done and putting continuing to tweet and watch
TV, there is a very good chance that Donald

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:21.440
Trump is going to really start taking his
anger out even more on media people that he

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:25.670
doesn't like, on politicians that he feels
haven't been supportive enough of him.

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:33.350
So I would expect a second term Trump will
really try to ruin people's lives, his enemies

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:37.950
lives, the people that he perceives as his
damaged enemies or not having been with him

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:42.700
while he mostly just rubber stamps, whatever
Republicans convinced him to do, it will be

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:43.890
very, very ugly.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.459
It will be very ugly.

00:03:45.459 --> 00:03:47.480
And it is of of course not.

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:52.520
I don't want to say renewed importance because
it's been of constant importance that we do

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:55.810
everything we can to remove this guy in November.

